{{wikipedia|Memoir}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|mémoire||memoir}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|memoria||memory}}; see [[memory]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɛmˌwɑr/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[autobiography]]; a book describing the [[personal]] experiences of an [[author]].
#: ''When I retire, I'm going to write my '''memoirs'''.''
# Any form of narrative describing the personal experiences of a writer.

====Usage notes====
* A memoir focuses around a mood or attitude toward a particular section of one's life. This differs from an [[autobiography]], which details the chronology, events, places, reactions, movements and any other relevant information that inhabited the life of the subject. Fact, above all, is the foundation of an autobiography. Remember, memoir is not just about what exactly happened in the past, but rather how it made you feel, and perhaps more importantly, how it makes you feel now.<ref>http://www.wordclay.com/genre/memoirautobiography.aspx</ref>

* The plural ''[[memoirs]]'' is very often used to refer to a single work.

====Related terms====
* [[memory]]

